id "q-127069" :question/id #uuid "2b4f7627-0162-5a60-8c0e-f1bcbe211fae" :question/math-academy-id "q-127069" :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the canonical equation $\\frac{x-4}{3}=\\frac{y-7}{-1}=\\frac{z+6}{-7}.$ Find the vector equation of the line." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-4}{3}=\\frac{y-7}{-1}=\\frac{z-(-6)}{-7},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(4,7,-6)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨3,-1,-7⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127069/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9927bff1-c245-542b-8d5d-fa7d24188b85"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127069"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32936/selection/00bc5b0e491764f97afda378152448460cc5ffeca1c6c90609a58d05ae0e3033" :answer/id #uuid "a214e0dd-c5f7-56c0-bcc3-0066251d066e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2t \\\\ y=t \\\\ z=t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32936/selection/ff80590883210d8278ea42b94a793dd5b07b207b2cce5585e26b6ea312e74bed" :answer/id #uuid "fc35b705-6ffd-552f-91d9-e64cdac2abf8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2t \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=3t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32936/selection/3b4b7419c074e7312c25fd5d762ddb0726c82d48a916d210e7dde86070c99515" :answer/id #uuid "7fa083d4-63e8-51d2-9073-2efef9626234" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2+2t \\\\ y=4+t \\\\ z=3-t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32936/selection/9d852017d74792803eecad344689107d98aaa498d6c438cba8dddaa10a2bd8f1" :answer/id #uuid "bbd7c90b-9b5c-5578-9d30-9ad89e8460df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=2+2t \\\\ y=1+4t \\\\ z=-1+3t\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32936/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "dc8eff61-2342-59ca-85df-e736f0507a5b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32936/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff32e8e6-b1fe-5d99-a72d-be93068c71c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32936/selection/9d852017d74792803eecad344689107d98aaa498d6c438cba8dddaa10a2bd8f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-32936/selection/00bc5b0e491764f97afda378152448460cc5ffeca1c6c90609a58d05ae0e3033" "q-32936/selection/ff80590883210d8278ea42b94a793dd5b07b207b2cce5585e26b6ea312e74bed" "q-32936/selection/3b4b7419c074e7312c25fd5d762ddb0726c82d48a916d210e7dde86070c99515" "q-32936/selection/9d852017d74792803eecad344689107d98aaa498d6c438cba8dddaa10a2bd8f1" "q-32936/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32936" :question/id #uuid "870015bf-07ab-5712-87fe-155681e8b5af" :question/math-academy-id "q-32936" :question/problem "Find the parametric equations of the line $\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y-1}{4}=\\frac{z+1}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{2}=\\frac{y-1}{4}=\\frac{z-(-1)}{3},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(2,1,-1)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨2,4,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=2+2t \\\\ y=1+4t \\\\ z=-1+3t\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32936/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9927bff1-c245-542b-8d5d-fa7d24188b85"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32936"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186120153 :question/answer-fields 17592186117438] {:db/id "q-33004/selection/ma-v1/d568231fb00dd6fcd36379e9c292e20245c96734be16ec054769fbd2b5afd99b/7d44c829f429d000e60deaf4d8c4881123b6d70e1f86de893346a08096375e47" :answer/id #uuid "1194370e-3a19-5f5f-a36e-23c23f28dee8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33004/selection/ma-v1/d568231fb00dd6fcd36379e9c292e20245c96734be16ec054769fbd2b5afd99b/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "34dff56a-5b79-5f15-b06d-9afe5e795a54" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33004/selection/ma-v1/d568231fb00dd6fcd36379e9c292e20245c96734be16ec054769fbd2b5afd99b/d2b94c141305c66b01983af934b8d1e50d101b4f8c3365e41d0801729d270d13" :answer/id #uuid "ff787d70-728d-58a2-bc05-0482309769a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "r=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\