\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ 5t \\\\ 6t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $P(2,5,-1)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨4,5,6⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{4}=\\frac{y-5}{5}=\\frac{z-(-1)}{6}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-2}{4}=\\frac{y-5}{5}=\\frac{z+1}{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-33006/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d44cf726-a4a6-5ac9-a63c-7464fe5566c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33006"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71029/selection/6a98878b5dd397a1f2976ec55d0ce0eb47981fd8804244eaf15fe4f057086da5" :answer/id #uuid "5fe979de-e2c4-5114-9b0c-54de6bb51621" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{4}=\\frac{y-4}{6}=\\frac{z+5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71029/selection/2501e78c1cac88027b1b7e4f35a0746b607c0ee26f180d92cad4aeb8fe89d1f9" :answer/id #uuid "7ee13250-3468-5dfc-8569-8e6f8e276ac4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}=\\frac{y}{6}=\\frac{z}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71029/selection/f76aea5e102801f2e75eceb296a43ec05a8deaf02a534a0d4f503b20dce026fd" :answer/id #uuid "af86d517-949c-5ba9-a5a3-19147a5d4af5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{4}=\\frac{y+4}{6}=\\frac{z-5}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71029/selection/f4a87de3f8a0ab10b656e9e5dc99ddbff693b24b7678a2c0292925c36db61b6