nfty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :question/worked-solution "We have the vector equation \n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $P(7,-2,4)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨1,-2,3⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{1}=\\frac{y-(-2)}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{1}=\\frac{y+2}{-2}=\\frac{z-4}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-127406/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d44cf726-a4a6-5ac9-a63c-7464fe5566c5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127406"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71045/selection/65e536123a5605edbaca7e6f47750a6b2527db883bf971028838889829cdd1e7" :answer/id #uuid "e3e6832e-a237-5195-9572-b03c4c67c919" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=z,\\,y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71045/selection/55d6736f53aa5646a704c9bceaacb955a6e5865648369e8ae87640e07386d2cc" :answer/id #uuid "d91c35e4-85f6-50c5-8c0c-4291a5d35c3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{-3}=\\frac{y+2}{5},\\,z=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71045/selection/b7483a15013a5e76d33e70c4b8f83fc96da7414df57569bf6fec9d321d8cd345" :answer/id #uuid "c85bc298-fef8-545e-b666-409ba57aa9f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y+5}{-2}=z,\\,x=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71045/selection/8b151f5ec69f4ae9926c1dcab8ab7b4cd679c4aca5cf962ae416505a912b07da" :answer/id #uuid "648dd039-a858-5c69-a71e-f821d1686183" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-5}{-2}=z,\\,x=-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71045/selection/32a5869f124f5755798340c3c204fc2c530a2cb54e69e142b04512cf17190521" :answer/id #uuid "6d1c67bc-934c-5683-a01b-521f263f411e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+3=\\frac{y-5}{-2}=z" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71045/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "80ef1a4e-9e9b-55a8-9c9e-de406d172759" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71045/selection/8b151f5ec69f4ae9926c1dcab8ab7b4cd679c4aca5cf962ae416505a912b07da" :answer-field/choices ["q-71045/selection/65e536123a5605edbaca7e6f47750a6b2527db883bf971028838889829cdd1e7" "q-71045/selection/55d6736f53aa5646a704c9bceaacb955a6e5865648369e8ae87640e07386d2cc" "q-71045/selection/b7483a15013a5e76d33e70c4b8f83fc96da7414df57569bf6fec9d321d8cd345" "q-71045/selection/8b151f5ec69f4ae9926c1dcab8ab7b4cd679c4aca5cf962ae416505a912b07da" "q-71045/selection/32a5869f124f5755798340c3c204fc2c530a2cb54e69e142b04512cf17190521"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71045" :question/id #uuid "5a54b426-ecf5-557b-8288-a133688ba386" :question/math-academy-id "q-71045" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-3)}{0}=\\frac{y-5}{-2}=\\frac{z-0}{1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{0}=\\frac{y-5}{-2}=z,\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{x+3}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $x$ component always maintains the constant value of $x=-3:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5-2t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{x+3}{0}$ part and instead write $x=-3,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{y-5}{-2}=z,\\,x=-3\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71045/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07c209a4-5c69-561e-9015-28b0f6e436e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71045"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127412/selection/57958577c6646be40d170501213f550a5d76fd0be7c05d026e444cd9e8dbb70e" :answer/id #uuid "c10e5aed-cf1c-5e07-8c83-9d1709baff68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{-2},\\,y=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127412/selection/9c9d7c1067f5d3ac832f9d05ab93a222815c51e000903b322e6b17071b03848e" :answer/id #uuid "11250407-1bd6-53c3-934a-a11d2358c2be" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{z+1}{-2},\\,y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127412/selection/c990bfe3482229c1645ada9177cc8666e0ae918ff7f2457625e06fc3d3849971" :answer/id #uuid "8b7943e9-bc79-5d8b-9d53-8f4dbe8253d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{-2},\\,y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127412/selection/9af1d0de9be4483f34b41a63622e2a211ec1de22b79d36275ccfc8380ec558f8" :answer/id #uuid "61bf33c7-cdc9-5ec0-969c-506bda763315" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{z+1}{-2},\\,y=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127412/selection/3e5169d74fe20b87a03eb61e8c64f3d3c0df7f1c0ed950c2695ed86fe4685873" :answer/id #uuid "e7a0ebd7-374d-5121-99f6-6de8e92fcb37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{-3}=\\frac{z-1}{2},\\,y=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127412/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cef0f500-ef18-57ed-939c-6c4b7927683d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127412/selection/c990bfe3482229c1645ada9177cc8666e0ae918ff7f2457625e06fc3d3849971" :answer-field/choices ["q-127412/selection/57958577c6646be40d170501213f550a5d76fd0be7c05d026e444cd9e8dbb70e" "q-127412/selection/9c9d7c1067f5d3ac832f9d05ab93a222815c51e000903b322e6b17071b03848e" "q-127412/selection/c990bfe3482229c1645ada9177cc8666e0ae918ff7f2457625e06fc3d3849971" "q-127412/selection/9af1d0de9be4483f34b41a63622e2a211ec1de22b79d36275ccfc8380ec558f8" "q-127412/selection/3e5169d74fe20b87a03eb61e8c64f3d3c0df7f1c0ed950c2695ed86fe4685873"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127412" :question/id #uuid "20898869-78be-5170-b137-d50ec6ffe709" :question/math-academy-id "q-127412" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-3)}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{0}=\\frac{z-1}{-2}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{0}=\\frac{z-1}{-2},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{y-2}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=2:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3+3t \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1-2t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{y-2}{0}$ part and instead write $y=2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{z-1}{-2},\\,y=2\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127412/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07c209a4-5c69-561e-9015-28b0f6e436e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71039/selection/ba7cd27d7a4e8b9483bed2e041b1cf8a575ec3b15edf80eb99c038d76df6ac75" :answer/id #uuid "a7ce48b2-2e7f-5dad-9ecc-1e06b048aec0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+9}{2}=z-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71039/selection/64bb0f9a440a4d4464975d0f16b2f0228b0df47f50f569f87294b7f41cbc0706" :answer/id #uuid "a590e034-4000-5b10-b34c-ec1b956e4c31" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-7}{-3}=z-11,\\,y=-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71039/selection/7658974130787558a61d929f36186f7332e1eba07af37095e715487b37ce3562" :answer/id #uuid "5deab0e9-6dbe-514b-bafb-bd27d1a64cc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+7}{-3}=\\frac{y-9}{2},\\,z=-11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71039/selection/448d3a03d8ceec18046ca11294e73304a1a9f629e29184448a35750f416be1f4" :answer/id #uuid "a6251438-70a2-5914-be4d-bab80d66ba4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+9}{2},\\,z=11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71039/selection/360734534c0258dfd1fb8891f85d6f287d1bfbf158b91b7b27be9601195b6b68" :answer/id #uuid "b1e755ad-e39b-5f0c-bb44-a4c932c7bfb3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{y-2}{-9},\\,z=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71039/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa2c10a-daa5-504b-a943-5f0ca58af690" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71039/selection/448d3a03d8ceec18046ca11294e73304a1a9f629e29184448a35750f416be1f4" :answer-field/choices ["q-71039/selection/ba7cd27d7a4e8b9483bed2e041b1cf8a575ec3b15edf80eb99c038d76df6ac75" "q-71039/selection/64bb0f9a440a4d4464975d0f16b2f0228b0df47f50f569f87294b7f41cbc0706" "q-71039/selection/7658974130787558a61d929f36186f7332e1eba07af37095e715487b37ce3562" "q-71039/selection/448d3a03d8ceec18046ca11294e73304a1a9f629e29184448a35750f416be1f4" "q-71039/selection/360734534c0258dfd1fb8891f85d6f287d1bfbf158b91b7b27be9601195b6b68"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71039" :question/id #uuid "12484b2b-517e-53da-82a8-68ef46a1747e" :question/math-academy-id "q-71039" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y-(-9)}{2}=\\frac{z-11}{0}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+9}{2}=\\frac{z-11}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{z-11}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=11:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}7-3t \\\\ -9+2t \\\\ 11\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z-11}{0}$ part and instead write $z=11$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-3}=\\frac{y+9}{2},\\,z=11\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71039/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07c209a4-5c69-561e-9015-28b0f6e436e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71039"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71048/selection/0511d509ba4992456488b1c10fe61a21306f01f1a378f353ec030dcd2ffd0338" :answer/id #uuid "cdf4a3a1-30a5-5dba-8526-3eb2a68d2150" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y+1}{-3},\\,z=6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71048/selection/1cf67a223e9993d3f916e88a6ef37c95780599b03c0274fbda6bd956fb461a69" :answer/id #uuid "51bbf9d7-ebb6-57d9-9db1-377f308a7ea3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-7}{3}=\\frac{y+3}{-1},\\,z=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71048/selection/08329cbecf7a6ced2859ddceb68489d5e2cbb9b0ae542dd0c6cdb2f4890843c9" :answer/id #uuid "f150c224-2fb0-5d8f-b8b0-53363c150bca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{y-1}{-3},\\,z=-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71048/selection/ad8afef0c1338f6614e86e63948046686fdd149136903015b23b8bcaa6ae67bb" :answer/id #uuid "d1e9c5bb-e8c2-5b1e-80ba-2229ed350480" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+7}{3}=\\frac{y-3}{-1},\\,z=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71048/selection/d9256df2b2a4804317a44d4827e6d5b985350bc022b1a1b50f4505dc04503b46" :answer/id #uuid "bf5b386d-4e12-559d-add5-c299c2ec74f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y+1}{-3}=z-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71048/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bba3a63e-a2b8-5a00-8c7b-3dad51c6269f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71048/selection/0511d509ba4992456488b1c10fe61a21306f01f1a378f353ec030dcd2ffd0338" :answer-field/choices ["q-71048/selection/0511d509ba4992456488b1c10fe61a21306f01f1a378f353ec030dcd2ffd0338" "q-71048/selection/1cf67a223e9993d3f916e88a6ef37c95780599b03c0274fbda6bd956fb461a69" "q-71048/selection/08329cbecf7a6ced2859ddceb68489d5e2cbb9b0ae542dd0c6cdb2f4890843c9" "q-71048/selection/ad8afef0c1338f6614e86e63948046686fdd149136903015b23b8bcaa6ae67bb" "q-71048/selection/d9256df2b2a4804317a44d4827e6d5b985350bc022b1a1b50f4505dc04503b46"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71048" :question/id #uuid "aa1fb4ff-b4b1-5558-a7f2-a6d8fc0b693f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71048" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y-(-1)}{-3}=\\frac{z-6}{0}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y+1}{-3}=\\frac{z-6}{0},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{z-6}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=6:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}3+7t \\\\ -1-3t \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z-6}{0}$ part and instead write $z=6$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{y+1}{-3},\\,z=6\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71048/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07c209a4-5c69-561e-9015-28b0f6e436e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71048"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127454/selection/0f3a63e2b437ae99af59117fc431a30bf18935e322a6584bddcdca712a8b5d67" :answer/id #uuid "65be7eab-e99a-5dd7-84c4-86d1cb996d6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{z-2}{2},\\,y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127454/selection/f0acf0449aca260ebb3598ef1d466d60517baca03b46345c5cb0ee7347f6666e" :answer/id #uuid "f8db0e3b-1195-5cce-b9df-f3d39fd777fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{z}{2},\\,y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127454/selection/25c9664bfcfe16ab7fbb24c5f4aefc350eebde2be1d04dc2a191db5b023de3fa" :answer/id #uuid "3318adcf-7bb9-5b0b-9756-1d6ffe1555d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{z}{2},\\,y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127454/selection/eee98c72e81859df7d654f21a28a5e50242f3fe66e0a4b9b10d593a5e22a443d" :answer/id #uuid "32ca8123-3590-52e8-b5f4-0371ac13228f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{7}=\\frac{z-2}{1},\\,y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127454/selection/4e7694d3d5f12318dd54cd065746e0cae21adb820a456978d703bd6d02feb14a" :answer/id #uuid "a8070fe3-83c6-5322-a070-c2eeffcc169c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{2}=\\frac{z}{7},\\,y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127454/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ad3b3c3c-4c60-5fe9-8882-4cf3947514ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127454/selection/f0acf0449aca260ebb3598ef1d466d60517baca03b46345c5cb0ee7347f6666e" :answer-field/choices ["q-127454/selection/0f3a63e2b437ae99af59117fc431a30bf18935e322a6584bddcdca712a8b5d67" "q-127454/selection/f0acf0449aca260ebb3598ef1d466d60517baca03b46345c5cb0ee7347f6666e" "q-127454/selection/25c9664bfcfe16ab7fbb24c5f4aefc350eebde2be1d04dc2a191db5b023de3fa" "q-127454/selection/eee98c72e81859df7d654f21a28a5e50242f3fe66e0a4b9b10d593a5e22a443d" "q-127454/selection/4e7694d3d5f12318dd54cd065746e0cae21adb820a456978d703bd6d02feb14a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127454" :question/id #uuid "25a771d1-622d-52c6-8734-39dc2e49e8c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-127454" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-3)}{7}=\\frac{y-5}{0}=\\frac{z}{2}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{y-5}{0}=\\frac{z}{2},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\frac{y-5}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=5:$\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3+7t \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2t\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{y-5}{0}$ part and instead write $y=5$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+3}{7}=\\frac{z}{2},\\,y=5\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127454/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07c209a4-5c69-561e-9015-28b0f6e436e5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127454"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-33249/selection/cdb8911cf0a01764b3deda7295cdea71d173a72459a06bba3017c265317d1c5b" :answer/id #uuid "acac261a-de6a-5bfb-8ca1-cc20367358c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{y+6}{-5}=\\frac{z+9}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33249/selection/fc7bf494a8ec4304a2e22334671f45cf8dbb66290fb1e009430c7c2674db29f0" :answer/id #uuid "05352976-ee1b-5b61-8232-9560a531693d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+3}{3}=\\frac{y-5}{6}=\\frac{z+7}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33249/selection/dc6697c2cbf55b818e00d6a1fc4aa545fe533833f3b0b1a3a272de247d4da758" :answer/id #uuid "cf4f9bf8-d08f-5bcf-83fc-db6813ae2de6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y-6}{-5}=\\frac{z-9}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33249/selection/7543f97487b3594662281a843b0e1ae3c3c57489a7bc3f53519a4247ce7ceefd" :answer/id #uuid "b38041ef-f5ad-5f98-835f-61500cd8f7fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y+5}{6}=\\frac{z-7}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33249/selection/7f1ddf8b2e4bf036b8a77ccb31a628fd04c4ff34db9e728cda86f815bc87c129" :answer/id #uuid "b0388943-ad11-526a-8826-03bfb44c15d8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{3}=\\frac{y}{6}=\\frac{z}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33249/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0055738-bf32-57e7-a545-67b369dd64b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33249/selection/7543f97487b3594662281a843b0e1ae3c3c57489a7bc3f53519a4247ce7ceefd" :answer-field/choices ["q-33249/selection/cdb8911cf0a01764b3deda7295cdea71d173a72459a06bba3017c265317d1c5b" "q-33249/selection/fc7bf494a8ec4304a2e22334671f45cf8dbb66290fb1e009430c7c2674db29f0" "q-33249/selection/dc6697c2cbf55b818e00d6a1fc4aa545fe533833f3b0b1a3a272de247d4da758" "q-33249/selection/7543f97487b3594662281a843b0e1ae3c3c57489a7bc3f53519a4247ce7ceefd" "q-33249/selection/7f1ddf8b2e4bf036b8a77ccb31a628fd04c4ff34db9e728cda86f815bc87c129"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33249" :question/id #uuid "3d46d489-a3da-58f9-8831-498d49fadfa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-33249" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the straight line that passes through $P(3,-5,7)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨3,6,9⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y-(-5)}{6}=\\frac{z-7}{9}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nor, equivalently,\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{3}=\\frac{y+5}{6}=\\frac{z-7}{9}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-33249/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc74baa-313b-51e7-8ae1-5e9fe0761256"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33249"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33234"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/1f9599192c1979f40fc519458019ed3296d9a5ef9048aaed41aab973c62e0be8.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-2,3,1)$ and $Q(5,-1,4).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨5,-1,4⟩-⟨-2,3,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,-4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-2)}{7}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-1}{3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+2}{7}=\\frac{y-3}{-4}=\\frac{z-1}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-127535/selection/8a28c0bac9e5b61ce4ff32eef60aa56de424e2dfed45d05bf5674a5b5f88148a" :answer/id #uuid "000edebc-1e5e-52b0-a9de-f20fe0034291" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{3},\\,z=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127535/selection/1549ac72e0c4a9baec240c2dc113222308287d0bc5d47aadc8fc414dca97d4c4" :answer/id #uuid "035a6874-6c4b-5495-a0cd-db32991e6815" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-7}{6}=\\frac{y-2}{3},\\,z=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127535/selection/c87d0dac764da7cb6eb166fa58c5ddc733611160e25d37e49583b467fff01d58" :answer/id #uuid "e1741111-296e-512c-8f6b-f8faf63425c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-7}{6}=\\frac{y-2}{3},\\,z=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127535/selection/7b34ed1f085eefeb3524896e170f352e9c4bb4c355412cbe9a274d2a4a8fcc92" :answer/id #uuid "a290a146-754d-5108-a099-f99363cd7ac6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+7}{-6}=\\frac{y-2}{-3},\\,z=-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127535/selection/adb8ba873285fc72f934d46c248c393d46bf6682ccac3bb681f07ef0ab2693e7" :answer/id #uuid "40116425-bfed-5f5a-ab95-3e4695a81e95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{-3},\\,z=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127535/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a25ad256-2afe-542f-bd14-1da74a18de5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127535/selection/8a28c0bac9e5b61ce4ff32eef60aa56de424e2dfed45d05bf5674a5b5f88148a" :answer-field/choices ["q-127535/selection/8a28c0bac9e5b61ce4ff32eef60aa56de424e2dfed45d05bf5674a5b5f88148a" "q-127535/selection/1549ac72e0c4a9baec240c2dc113222308287d0bc5d47aadc8fc414dca97d4c4" "q-127535/selection/c87d0dac764da7cb6eb166fa58c5ddc733611160e25d37e49583b467fff01d58" "q-127535/selection/7b34ed1f085eefeb3524896e170f352e9c4bb4c355412cbe9a274d2a4a8fcc92" "q-127535/selection/adb8ba873285fc72f934d46c248c393d46bf6682ccac3bb681f07ef0ab2693e7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127535" :question/id #uuid "ec5e4c78-d2dc-529b-bc3a-14014c27c99d" :question/math-academy-id "q-127535" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/44b0b683358bb448229380402717f396d13f82d2904bbf1ece1fcf9fd4567f14.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points $P(7,-2,4)$ and $Q(1,1,4).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,4⟩-⟨7,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,3,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y-(-2)}{3}=\\frac{z-4}{0}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{3}=\\frac{z-4}{0}.\n$$\n\nBut the above equation is problematic because $\\frac{z-4}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, in our line, the $z$ component always maintains the constant value of $z=4.$ For example, our two points $P(7,-2,4)$ and $Q(1,1,4)$ both have $z$-coordinates of $z=4.$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{z-4}{0}$ part and instead write $z=4,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-7}{-6}=\\frac{y+2}{3},\\,z=4\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-127535/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc74baa-313b-51e7-8ae1-5e9fe0761256"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127535"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-32827/selection/4cf3601b45c03c5825e96b13277e8888a287be2d9e249692788bcc837e1a9665" :answer/id #uuid "15dcdc34-f585-5a5d-bc6d-8262b77214a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-3}{-1}=\\frac{z+1}{3},\\,x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32827/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" :answer/id #uuid "3de067b2-e829-592b-81db-c3a3b6247b95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None of the listed" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32827/selection/e428e9f064247602a526707848dc19bdc851936f4cbed9ae5e5085d2eb3cd18f" :answer/id #uuid "e2e251b1-26b5-5b29-b7fe-725714d987b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{y-3}{-1}=\\frac{z+1}{3},\\,x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32827/selection/22c5d68805421467acb3d2bfe0471065351a4acc18d643537d5ddf9418f9409e" :answer/id #uuid "512a8197-caa7-5eab-b7c7-66a1191f39a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{3}=\\frac{z-3}{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32827/selection/23aa27fa5db636c3dcbc5ace4c8833a34d9fa6e63c0a108439e63e777da830c7" :answer/id #uuid "95225742-41f4-5f84-8597-065439478393" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{2}=\\frac{y}{3}=\\frac{z}{-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-32827/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "eb47a688-ab4b-5fef-8e62-4ec8473de07c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-32827/selection/22c5d68805421467acb3d2bfe0471065351a4acc18d643537d5ddf9418f9409e" :answer-field/choices ["q-32827/selection/4cf3601b45c03c5825e96b13277e8888a287be2d9e249692788bcc837e1a9665" "q-32827/selection/421ba3cf61c86c7d854403490925f53920cd3c015c12342698571d9a74aca2fd" "q-32827/selection/e428e9f064247602a526707848dc19bdc851936f4cbed9ae5e5085d2eb3cd18f" "q-32827/selection/22c5d68805421467acb3d2bfe0471065351a4acc18d643537d5ddf9418f9409e" "q-32827/selection/23aa27fa5db636c3dcbc5ace4c8833a34d9fa6e63c0a108439e63e777da830c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32827" :question/id #uuid "ba3c810b-166e-5700-9ed9-2bd016f2db70" :question/math-academy-id "q-32827" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the straight line that passes through $P(0,-1,3)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨2,3,-1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-0}{2}=\\frac{y-(-1)}{3}=\\frac{z-3}{-1}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{2}=\\frac{y+1}{3}=\\frac{z-3}{-1}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-32827/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc74baa-313b-51e7-8ae1-5e9fe0761256"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32827"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71030/selection/f8620b94b8ed9fb460696549739552a369ee32af207a35efdb3418775beb26ba" :answer/id #uuid "2fb75d30-8f29-58ea-b094-f7b263390113" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-9}{4}=\\frac{y-3}{-5}=\\frac{z+7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71030/selection/8024bd948a78a83fed1a0b2b866a36d1f4e8ee1ddd29cd0f61d112c37f2b2aad" :answer/id #uuid "99d6eebf-7242-5454-8408-a833ab3b3442" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+9}{4}=\\frac{y+3}{-5}=\\frac{z-7}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71030/selection/857ab4038781b1f7e1a21de6f8f75f4ee8107757f31114699d1ceb389a366ad9" :answer/id #uuid "4a920040-c93b-5d7a-bab2-67007d717d6b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4}=\\frac{y}{-5}=\\frac{z}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71030/selection/9d2010fe3d0fb8c3398080c7ddb8d94c73d91821dbfaf32de865c9b9ed260044" :answer/id #uuid "3c3a56cf-9179-5758-801c-2898b6f9fab8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x+4}{9}=\\frac{y-5}{3}=\\frac{z+3}{-7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71030/selection/0ad6f75b62efd549b3a795c559f865c99125518bd6a05d9607abc216ecbd37f4" :answer/id #uuid "e84de808-3692-524b-813b-321d10c0a09b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x-4}{9}=\\frac{y+5}{3}=\\frac{z-3}{-7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71030/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9a0e5313-74b4-5137-862e-04fc9543ef40" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71030/selection/f8620b94b8ed9fb460696549739552a369ee32af207a35efdb3418775beb26ba" :answer-field/choices ["q-71030/selection/f8620b94b8ed9fb460696549739552a369ee32af207a35efdb3418775beb26ba" "q-71030/selection/8024bd948a78a83fed1a0b2b866a36d1f4e8ee1ddd29cd0f61d112c37f2b2aad" "q-71030/selection/857ab4038781b1f7e1a21de6f8f75f4ee8107757f31114699d1ceb389a366ad9" "q-71030/selection/9d2010fe3d0fb8c3398080c7ddb8d94c73d91821dbfaf32de865c9b9ed260044" "q-71030/selection/0ad6f75b62efd549b3a795c559f865c99125518bd6a05d9607abc216ecbd37f4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71030" :question/id #uuid "67dee0f1-a305-5544-8b63-7dcdcefbb7bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-71030" :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the straight line that passes through $P(9,3,-7)$ and is parallel to $v=⟨4,-5,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨{v}_{x},{v}_{y},{v}_{z}⟩$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-{x}_{0}}{{v}_{x}}=\\frac{y-{y}_{0}}{{v}_{y}}=\\frac{z-{z}_{0}}{{v}_{z}}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-9}{4}=\\frac{y-3}{-5}=\\frac{z-(-7)}{3}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-9}{4}=\\frac{y-3}{-5}=\\frac{z+7}{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71030/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cbc74baa-313b-51e7-8ae1-5e9fe0761256"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71030"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4910"] :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the canonical equation $\\dfrac{x}{5}=\\dfrac{y+3}{3}=\\dfrac{z-2}{1}.$ Find the vector equation of the line." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the straight line that passes through the point $P(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ and is parallel to the vector $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle v_x, v_y, v_z \\rangle$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-x_0}{v_x}=\\dfrac{y-y_0}{v_y}=\\dfrac{z-z_0}{v_z} = t, \\qquad t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\nComparing the above to our given equation\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{5}=\\dfrac{y-(-3)}{3}=\\dfrac{z-2}{1},\n$$\n\nwe find that our line passes through the point $P(0,-3,2)$ and is parallel to $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle 5,3,1 \\rangle.$ Therefore, its vector equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4911"] :question/problem "Consider the straight line with the parametric equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1-2t \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=-2+3t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1-2t \\\\ 4t \\\\ -2+3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2t \\\\ 4t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nThis implies that the given line passes through the point $P(1,0,-2)$ and is parallel to the vector $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle -2, 4, 3 \\rangle.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{-2}=\\dfrac{y}{4}=\\dfrac{z-(-2)}{3} = t, \t\\qquad t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{-2}=\\dfrac{y}{4}=\\dfrac{z+2}{3}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5021"] :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation for the line with the following vector equation:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/fea24c391122278ffe20ec0f6a7d704b835aca18c3bdcd7395aeeea0f593a2bf.png)" :question/worked-solution "Using the usual formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{4}=\\dfrac{y-2}{0}=\\dfrac{z-3}{5} = t,\t\\qquad t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{4}=\\dfrac{y-2}{0}=\\dfrac{z-3}{5},\n$$\n\nwhich is problematic because $\\dfrac{y-2}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, notice that in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=2\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/368f42200b9366547bdff9840a894b63d3df43722052ecb1a4e15e2306b4e56a.png)\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\dfrac{y-2}{0}$ part and instead write $y=2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x-1}{4}=\\dfrac{z-3}{5}, \\; y=2\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4912"] :question/problem "Find a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/792bf09ff2546903b863a879a2518c42bbd30fdfce652bd4e22b1ad19aefc7c9.png)" :question/worked-solution "We know that the line passes through the points ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/bf6bd67f4c98a8d36673d51a9fd9ee42ce53c45dcd793e19b36796908be0dfca.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/80d08830e9c7790842989560740c1a8c09a2cf794399799fa44f0bfd302f165a.png) Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/54f43a22493f78d42649844a6e360d5226cc8cb7c19af11c8e8b595354063789.png) which is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/9eec5064637ab51b30b8bcae7d33babac63edd10da36315ab18c61da76f7b102.png)\n\nUsing the point ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/c9b75fa5f325825788ae2a64e227779c81af2454230ded498d7245dd9e0c66cf.png) and the vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/dee4f9a47a1bdff7b5bee4b328768e8967ff52dba70800b6defa0575a7034847.png), we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/fdf49c280c1dcb705153d75b3f52527d7a3d6e5be88fc2497d69553ea9de953b.png)\nor equivalently\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/d606ca3e74d93f6a3e4d802603a1b27729301cd7b9611ed94d0514a6a2997f4b.png)\n\nBut the above equation is problematic because ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/7153fc0366e9f632513e320313657591fe8f5a4238f1f0987ada184183e462ac.png) involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, in our line, the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/d0a37c7a07a4a5e017e3edb659fad8defff4fa33a3accbd0e6fd2d6d8439cf94.png) component always maintains the constant value ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/b7f9100157159abea8f5f7a86a272d5a539e2d8084e8c894642bc49342e2a76f.png) For example, our two points ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/ad5d9528b6a85fa9d0e010a6c7b0fe7d51253b71fe995a2010204708256aa081.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/5a762bf2a30c7fb3be3ba2e1d8abf1b308614d123e11600d93d7b3b02fe828c7.png) both have ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/fdc688a7d7010425aace3db801008b0b83b950e7ff7c03a89f9745d4651e1dca.png)-coordinates of ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/9626663f5000cd7c8c37eeec3c498de49124f3cc6807fcaf713b85e6a692a595.png)\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/7ff8eda495247902c9dfd90af00e4544a0090cab531689e7b7a833bce66fd9ac.png) part and instead write ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/f0d48b15791c63393dea1717a24819d4ba7502f28b54a363f5c9890b0bdb1079.png) as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042625/assets/41d29b651c736cf13b6cbde92ffc46ae33bfb3e139ebec8aff2f7c05f431fde7.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
